==English==

===Noun===
'''men's'''

# {{form of|possessive case|[[men]]}}
# The [[men's room]]; the [[bathroom]] in a public or commercial establishment reserved for [[male]]s.
# A [[store]] [[department]] where [[clothing]] is sold for adult males.

====Usage notes====
* Contrast this form with "man's". Man, used as a [[collective noun]], refers to [[mankind]]. "Man's" refers to properties of mankind, usually of all genders. Men (often referring to males) is a simple plural.

